<title>USA: Wait and see on Brazil-US soybeans - USDA official.</title>
<headline>Wait and see on Brazil-US soybeans - USDA official.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department has &quot;no particular projections&quot; for Brazilian soybean sales to U.S. buyers, a USDA official said Tuesday, noting one purported sale had not materialized.</p>
<p>&quot;We don't know at this point if, in fact, any Brazilian soybeans will be imported,&quot; said Chris Goldthwait, USDA sales manager.</p>
<p>USDA has projected U.S. soybean imports of 120,000 tonnes during 1996/97, roughly the same as previous years. USDA will update its trade forecasts on Friday with its April edition of the World Agrcultural Supply and Demand Estimates report.</p>
</text>
